      "content": "Thanks, that's actually a really good start. It reads very professionally and you used the keywords naturally without making it sound like a list.\n\nI just ran it through our internal tool to see where we stand, and the score came back as 11. It's okay, but our benchmark for \"high-quality\" content usually sits closer to 20 or 25. \n\nI really don't want you to start keyword-stuffing or making the sentences weird just to pump that number up because, like I said, if it looks fake to a human, it's a fail. But, if there's a way to expand on the analysis—maybe add a bit more detail on the emerging markets or the energy sector—and weave those terms in more effectively to get that score up closer to the benchmark, that would be great. Could you try an expanded version?",
